  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.752pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(55.32pt, 261.3pt, "Abstract")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.752pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.56pt, 261.3pt, "—In ambient electromagnetic energy harvesting ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 271.32pt, "systems, the input power to the rectifier is low. To improve ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 281.339pt, "rectification efficiency, Schottky diodes, which are sensitive to low ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 291.479pt, "power, are commonly selected as rectifying devices to convert ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 301.499pt, "microwave power into dc power. However, low-power rectifying ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 311.579pt, "diodes typically have low reverse breakdown voltages, making ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 321.599pt, "them susceptible to reverse breakdown under high power ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 331.739pt, "conditions. This letter proposes a low-power rectifier with ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 341.759pt, "reconfigurable function. The rectifying diode is connected in ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 351.839pt, "parallel with the PIN diode. At low input power, the output dc ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 361.859pt, "voltage is low, and the PIN diode remains off, having no impact on ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 371.999pt, "the rectifier’s operation. As the input power increases, the PIN ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 382.018pt, "diode turns on, causing change in circuit structure and impedance ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 392.038pt, "mismatch. This leads to increased reflected power, thereby ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 402.119pt, "preventing the rectifying diode from receiving excessive power. ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 412.199pt, "Additionally, the turn-on voltage of the PIN diode is lower than ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 422.279pt, "the reverse breakdown voltage of the rectifying diode, protecting ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 432.299pt, "it from reverse breakdown. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.752pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(55.32pt, 454.079pt, "Index Terms")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.752pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(103.92pt, 454.079pt, "—PIN diode, rectifier, reconfigurable function, ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 464.099pt, "reverse breakdown. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.744pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(132pt, 486.78pt, "I.")
  #line-at(144.66pt, 486.78pt, "I")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.76pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(147.9pt, 486.78pt, "NTRODUCTION")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.744pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(71.219pt, 501.84pt, "ith the rapid development of wireless communication ")
  #line-at(71.219pt, 513.059pt, "technologies, the amount of electromagnetic energy in ")
  #line-at(71.219pt, 524.22pt, "the environment is increasing. At the same time, a large ")
  #line-at(45.539pt, 535.439pt, "number of wireless sensors are being used in the Internet of ")
  #line-at(45.539pt, 546.539pt, "Things (IoT). Currently, most wireless sensors are powered by ")
  #line-at(45.539pt, 557.759pt, "batteries, and their ability to function normally is dependent on ")
  #line-at(45.539pt, 568.979pt, "battery life. Regularly replacing batteries leads to increased ")
  #line-at(45.539pt, 580.078pt, "costs and pollution issues. Additionally, some wireless sensors ")
  #line-at(45.539pt, 591.298pt, "are located in areas that are inaccessible to humans, making ")
  #line-at(45.539pt, 602.518pt, "battery ")
  #line-at(86.407pt, 602.518pt, "replacement ")
  #line-at(147.739pt, 602.518pt, "difficult. ")
  #line-at(195.486pt, 602.518pt, "Therefore, ")
  #line-at(250.131pt, 602.518pt, "harvesting ")
  #line-at(45.539pt, 613.678pt, "electromagnetic energy from the environment to power ")
  #line-at(45.539pt, 624.838pt, "wireless sensors could effectively address the power supply ")
  #line-at(45.539pt, 636.058pt, "issue of these wireless sensors[1][2]. ")
  #line-at(55.32pt, 647.278pt, "Rectifiers can convert microwave power into dc power ")
  #line-at(45.539pt, 658.978pt, "[3][4][5], and are the core component of an electromagnetic ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.76pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.52pt, 691.32pt, "Manuscript received ")
  #set text(font: "DengXian", size: 7.76pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
