  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.744pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.56pt, 250.62pt, "energy harvesting system. Given that the energy density of ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 262.379pt, "electromagnetic waves in the environment is relatively low, the ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 274.139pt, "power input to the rectifier is also low. In order to achieve high ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 285.839pt, "conversion efficiency at low power levels, rectifying diodes are ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 297.599pt, "typically very sensitive to power. However, when close to a ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 309.36pt, "signal source, the received power increases rapidly, causing the ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 321.12pt, "rectifier's output voltage to rise. This may result in the ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 332.82pt, "rectifying diode being reverse-biased beyond its breakdown ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 344.581pt, "voltage, leading to the failure of the rectifier, as shown in Fig. 1. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 5.446pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(378pt, 432.72pt, "Wireless ")
  #line-at(380.1pt, 438.06pt, "Sensor")
  #line-at(454.201pt, 425.16pt, "Wireless ")
  #line-at(456.301pt, 430.5pt, "Sensor")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.76pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.56pt, 467.28pt, "Fig. 1. Electromagnetic energy harvesting powers wireless sensors. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.744pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(314.4pt, 489.72pt, "Some researchers have employed switches or additional ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 501.54pt, "rectifying diodes to increase the reverse breakdown voltage of ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 513.24pt, "the rectifying diodes. In [6], By using FET switches to ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 524.94pt, "reconfigure the rectifier, the reverse breakdown voltage of the ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 536.7pt, "diode is increased in the rectifier. Ref. [7] proposed a ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 548.461pt, "synergistic structure that introduces a high-power diode in front ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 560.221pt, "of the low-power diode to prevent it from breakdown. A ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 571.922pt, "recently proposed power-adaptive distribution structure ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 583.682pt, "enables the low-power rectifying diode to operate under ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 595.443pt, "low-power conditions, while the high-power rectifying diode ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 607.203pt, "functions under high-power conditions[8]. ")
  #line-at(314.4pt, 618.903pt, "Currently, there is limited research on the protection of ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 630.664pt, "low-power ")
  #line-at(358.1pt, 630.664pt, "rectifiers. ")
  #line-at(406.372pt, 630.664pt, "This ")
  #line-at(435.114pt, 630.664pt, "letter ")
  #line-at(466.438pt, 630.664pt, "proposes ")
  #line-at(512.425pt, 630.664pt, "a ")
  #line-at(528.084pt, 630.664pt, "novel ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 642.364pt, "reconfigurable mechanism for low-power rectifying diodes by ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 654.184pt, "introducing a PIN diode as a dc switch. This mechanism ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 665.884pt, "adaptively adjusts the switch based on the output voltage. ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 677.644pt, "When the PIN diode is turned on, the circuit structure is ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 689.344pt, "reconfigured, causing impedance mismatch. This prevents high ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 701.105pt, "input power from reaching the rectifying diode, protecting it ")
  #line-at(304.56pt, 712.866pt, "from damage. ")
