  #line-at(45.54pt, 93.9pt, "conventional and straightforward approach is to introduce a ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 105.6pt, "limiter. As shown in Fig. 2(a), when the input microwave ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 117.359pt, "power exceeds a certain threshold, the output microwave power ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 129.119pt, "remains constant, thereby protecting the subsequent circuits. ")
  #line-at(55.32pt, 140.879pt, "Different from the traditional design method, this letter ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 152.579pt, "proposes a novel circuit structure that utilizes an adaptive ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 164.279pt, "structure regulation mechanism to control the power entering ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 176.099pt, "the rectifying diode and the output dc voltage, as shown in Fig. ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 187.799pt, "2 (b). The switch state of the voltage-controlled component ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 199.559pt, "depends on the voltage across it. This component is connected ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 211.259pt, "in parallel with the rectifying diode. When the input power is ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 223.079pt, "low, the output dc voltage remains low, keeping the ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 234.779pt, "voltage-controlled component in the off state and leaving the ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 246.54pt, "rectifier's operation unaffected. As the input power gradually ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 258.24pt, "increases and the output dc voltage rises, the voltage-controlled ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 269.999pt, "component ")
  #line-at(99.384pt, 269.999pt, "turns ")
  #line-at(129.576pt, 269.999pt, "on, ")
  #line-at(152.352pt, 269.999pt, "restructuring ")
  #line-at(212.81pt, 269.999pt, "the ")
  #line-at(235.38pt, 269.999pt, "circuit. ")
  #line-at(273.346pt, 269.999pt, "This ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 281.759pt, "reconfiguration causes impedance mismatch and increased ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 293.518pt, "reflection, preventing excessive power from reaching the ")
  #line-at(45.54pt, 305.218pt, "rectifying diode.  ")
